[Music]  my name is kylie eckert  and the disease i chose is autosomal  dominant polycystic kidney disease  also known as pkd or polycystic kidney  disease  what is pkd pkd is caused by a mutation  in the pkd1 gene  although in more rare circumstances it  can be caused by  mutations in the pkd2 gene  and or um mutations in the protein  polycystin mutations in the pkd1 gene  cause  growth of cysts on the kidneys leading  to kidney failure in  approximately the fifth decade of life  however it affects  it can affect people between the ages of  0 and 80.  it is the most common common monogenic  kidney disease  and it affects over 12 million people  worldwide  the primary unit pro accession number is  displayed on the screen  there were two other uniproduct session  numbers however  they did not have any relevant  information to this presentation  the information from the primary  uniprice entry is reliable because it  was manually reviewed by swiss prop  it has a 5 out of 5 annotation score and  it has experimental evidence at the  protein level  pkd1 is located on human chromosome 16.  the only disease that pkd1 is implicated  in is autosomal dominant polycystic  kidney disease and the honor id of pkd  is number one seven three  nine zero zero  the pdb id for pkd  is 1b4r 1b4r  is actually the number for polycystin  one which is the protein  produced by the pkd1 gene  because there was only one reviewed  entry  in uniprot for pkd1 genes  i blasted all sequences that had greater  than 90  identity so that i would at least have  some results and a phylogenetic tree  these are diagrams the one on the left  is the human  poly pkd1 pkd2 complex and the one on  the right  is the human polycystin one complex  polycystin one is the protein produced  by the gene  pkd1  also there are no ligand interactions  for this complex  on scop i found the family super family  fold and class these this is all  class information for polycystin one  the protein they're all beta proteins  and just folded in an immunoglobulin  globulin like beta sandwich  in pymol i was unable to  pull up and fetch one b4r  which is polycysteine one so i modeled  pkd1 pkd2  the top picture is the complete  structure of the complex  the middle is zoomed in to show where  the mutation is which is right here  and the bottom picture is a magnified  picture of the  mutated amino ac the mutation that i  chose  is in position 3285  it causes polycystic kidney disease and  it's a change from  valene to isoleucine i  found this mutation by comparing a list  of pathological and disease implicated  mutations  in uniprot to the available mutations  in the mutation wizard in pymol  for the electrostatic model i was unable  to find an electrostatic  um structure online and in pymol for the  pkd1 pk22 complex  the error message that i found is on the  left here  but i was able to find an electrostatic  model of the 1v4r  or polycysteine 1 complex  finally these are my works cited thank  you

